# Wolseley Wasp four-door saloon, 1935-1936.
#
# The 1,069 cc Wasp: the small Wolseley of 1935-36, with the Wolseley grille
# and the six-light body. The research corrected the order's date: the Wasp
# is 1935-36, NOT 1955-56. 5,815 built.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wolseley_Wasp
#
# Dimensions 3.500 x 1.460 x 1.57 m, wheelbase 2.300 m. The height is an
# estimate; no published figure was established.
#
# Shape reference: NO true side profile exists. Image 1 is a front
# three-quarter of the 1935 car, registration CEH 14; the flank is estimated
# from it and the other views. The limitation is recorded.
#
# Colours: grade (d); no period chart was found. Black, grey, green and
# maroon are plain names. Weights 4, 3, 3, 2, total 12, provisional.
#
# Speed 110 km/h. Comfort 45/398, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 45. Classes 2,3.
# Dates are road presence: 1935 intro, retires staggered 1953-1956.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/wolseley-wasp.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/wolseley-wasp.dae. References:
# citycars/references/wolseley-wasp/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: there is no true side or rear view, so the flank and rear
# fittings are inferred; the model height of 1.57 m is an estimate. The roof sign
# on the ex-police car is omitted, and the wing-to-running-board transitions are
# simplified. At 128 px the small six-light body and Wolseley grille read as a
# Wasp.


obj=citycar
